+# Newcomer FAQ
+
+## How do I install the command line tool?
+
+Install it with pipx (Python 3.11 or newer): `pipx install tally-toolkit`. Check it with `tallyctl version`. If the
+command is not found, run `pipx ensurepath` and open a new terminal.
+
+## What is the tool called now?
+
+`tallyctl`. It was `tally-cli` until the 2026-09 release; the old name works as an alias for one more release, then
+goes away.
+
+## Which port does tally listen on?
+
+8731. The old port 8080 is closed, so anything still using it gets a refused connection.
+
+## How do I clear the cache?
+
+Run `tallyctl cache clear`. It clears all regions; add `--region NAME` for just one. The old purge command was removed.
+
+## How long until an unanswered page escalates?
+
+15 minutes without acknowledgement. It goes from the primary on-call to the secondary, then to the engineering manager.
+
+## Does the pager wake me at night?
+
+Only for severity 1: customer-facing data loss or a full outage. Between 22:00 and 07:00, severity 2 incidents, such as
+a slow dashboard or a delayed batch, wait for the morning. Pages arrive in the Beacon app; install it and log in with
+SSO before your first shift.
+
+## What do I do when the ingest queue is stuck?
+
+Run `tallyctl restart ingest --drain` first and look for the cause afterwards. It finishes in-flight work, parks the
+stuck batch in the dead-letter table and starts the consumer clean. A plain restart does not help.
+
+## What do I do when the API certificate has expired?
+
+Run `tallyctl certs renew api`, then `tallyctl restart api`: the new certificate is only served after the restart.
+`tallyctl certs list` shows expiry dates.
